[Music]  well the number of new  daily coronavirus infections in tokyo  has gone above 5000 for the first time  ever cases in the olympics host city are  rising  faster than ever fuelled by the more  contagious delta variant  more widely japan's government has  extended emergency measures to eight  more regions here's the data from johns  hopkins university this is the last 30  days in tokyo alone so 30 days ago we  were looking at approximately 500 new  cases a day  when the games started around 900  bringing us now  two weeks later to the point where there  are 5 000 plus  cases a day and then more widely this  is japan not just tokyo the whole  country since the start  of the year and just as a point of  reference  the olympic games began at this point  and i think the graph kind of tells the  story uh past  that andy richardson our correspondent  in tokyo it was not long ago  andy that olympics organizers were  saying that their games had nothing to  do with the rising cases across japan it  would be hard to argue that now  they are going to try and argue though i  can assure you uh kamal i mean  you were putting those figures into some  sort of context i was standing here last  week saying  figures in tokyo have hit 3000 um for  the first time that was a new record  then and the fact we've hit 5000 today  shows just how quickly  um this situation is escalating the  state of emergency uh just a few days  ago was extended  um here in tokyo until at least uh the  end of the month from  from a sporting perspective if that  really matters and that was going to  have an impact on the paralympic games  because there had been hopes that  spectators and fans could be allowed in  for the start of the paralympics  there's still a chance that that could  be the situation for the last few days  of that event but it all looks  um increasingly unlikely now and i think  there is a growing sense of frustration  amongst many people here we've spoken to  the vaccination rollout was slow the  back story there is that in the 1990s  the japanese government was hit with a  number of libel cases and was found  liable for side effects from other  inoculations so it was a very cautious  rollout of the vaccine and that's now  having an impact with this new  delta variants uh surging all over the  country it's not  just an issue in tokyo it is all over  the country and i think  the state of emergency itself is is a  bit of an oxymoron because it's it's not  a law or an order it is a request for  people to perhaps stay at home work from  home if they can  it's a request for restaurants to close  early and perhaps not surprisingly  um people are maybe not adhering to  those requests  when that same government is also  carrying on with the olympics  andy can you give us any indication of  what things are like actually in the  olympic village which  is really supposed to be the heart of  the bubble which is supposed to keep  this virus contained  that's right i mean every day you will  hear  the high number of screening tests  they've done the low number of positive  cases  and they will repeat that there is no  link no provable link between  the athletes village and what is  happening there and and the wider surges  in tokyo and around the rest of the  country there were 31 new cases  today what's interesting about  the breakdown of that number is that 23  were residents  of tokyo residents of japan either  working as contractors or volunteers  they're not staying in the athletes  village so this idea that there's  no chance of there being a link between  a positive case  in the village and in the wider  community is increasingly difficult  to maintain they say that  it's a big tv event the olympics and  it's actually encouraging people to  follow the state of emergency because of  the high tv ratings and it's encouraging  people to stay at home rather than go  out because obviously  no fans are allowed at the venues but  there is a frustration  there's a frustration amongst  epidemiologists not just amongst the  public  um that at a time when uh  the delta variant is surging that the  fact the games are going on is sending  out the wrong message it's sending out a  message of  optimism that you can relax and people  aren't  aware because of the fact the olympics  are going on just how serious  the situation is becoming in tokyo and  in in the wider country as well  andy richardson with that update from  the olympic games host city tokyo thank  you  we'll stay in asia

